  "notes": "REDESIGNED 2026-08-27 onto the simple pair; the halfplane version was never run and its dataset is retired. The full plan lives in notebooks/experiments/exp2_arch_sweep.ipynb: step 0 (minimal architectures, measured) then tasks A-F.\nMinimal architectures from step 0: simple_relevant is width 3 at ANY depth (practical minimum w3 d2 = 6 neurons; w3 d1 costs 2439 epochs against 111), simple_irrelevant is w1 d1 = 1 neuron. The reference w5 d5 is therefore 8.3x excess in neurons for one task and 25x for the other -- the same cell means different excess, and that is the content of the axis.\nWidth 1 and 2 exist on simple_irrelevant ONLY: on the relevant task no net of width <= 2 reaches 100 % at any depth (0 successes over 180 seeds), because every level set of a network whose widths are all <= input dimension is unbounded (Johnson, ICLR 2019), so a bounded decision region -- a disk inside a circle -- is unreachable. Those cells are the validity check the instrument must answer with exactly zero witnesses.\nStage 2 and stage 3 run through training/parallel_train.py and analysis/parallel_eval.py: both are resumable and both shard across processes. Sequential cost of the pool is ~6 h of evaluation, ~16 min on 32 workers."
